# Deploy PAWCAT after updates

Remote: `https://github.com/NeverSMILE0825/PAWCAT.git`  
Live site: `https://neversmile0825.github.io/PAWCAT/`

GitHub Pages is served from the `main` branch root. Pushing to `main` republishes automatically (no Actions workflow required).

Whenever you finish meaningful website changes in this project:

1. Commit the relevant files (user has requested ongoing deploy; commit + push after site updates unless they say not to).
2. `git push origin main`.
3. Briefly confirm Pages is updating / site is reachable.
4. Tell the user the live URL so they can verify.

Do not force-push to `main` unless the user explicitly asks.
Use `"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Programs\GitHubCLI\gh.exe"` for `gh` on this machine (npm `gh` is the wrong package).
